      "id": "claim_a95d0ee895a549a2bce642c368580ed6",
      "statement": "The Casbin model is a flat ACL whose matcher is exact subject equality with wildcards only on object/action (m = r.sub == p.sub && (p.obj == \"*\" || r.obj == p.obj) && (p.act == \"*\" || r.act == p.act)) — there is no subject wildcard and no role hierarchy, so each role needs its own policy rows, with p, ADMIN, *, * as the single wildcard grant.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/src/casbin/model.conf#L10-L11",
